  "id": "twin-control",
  "term": "twin control",
  "definition": "Twin control is a research design that compares twins who differ on a trait or exposure so researchers can examine its links with outcomes while accounting for factors the twins share. In a co-twin control design, those shared factors include genetic background and aspects of the environment.",
